Replace react-query-auth with Data Client in src/lib/auth.tsx. Today it is:

```ts
export const { useUser, useLogin, useLogout, useRegister, AuthLoader } = configureAuth({
  userFn: () => api.get('/auth/me').then((r) => r.data),
  loginFn: async (data: LoginInput) => (await api.post('/auth/login', data)).user,
  registerFn: async (data: RegisterInput) => (await api.post('/auth/register', data)).user,
  logoutFn: () => api.post('/auth/logout'),
});
```

`/auth/me` returns `{ data: User }`, login and register return `{ user: User, jwt: string }`. `AuthLoader` wraps the app in provider.tsx; components call `useUser().data`, `useLogin({ onSuccess }).mutate(values)` and `useLogout().mutate()`. A `User` Entity exists in src/api/user.ts and an `ApiEndpoint` base class in src/lib/api-client.ts.

